  "result": "Perfect! \u2713 All dashboard tests pass. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n**Dashboard Function Implementation:**\n\nThe `dashboard(invoices, asOf)` function returns comprehensive summary statistics:\n\n- **counts**: Breakdown of invoices per status (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- **outstanding**: Total amount still due on issued and partially_paid invoices\n- **overdue**: Object with { count, amount } showing number of overdue invoices and total overdue amount\n- **topCustomers**: Array of top 3 customers with most due, sorted highest first\n\n**Tests Added:** 10 comprehensive dashboard tests covering:\n- Empty invoice array\n- Invoice status counting\n- Outstanding amount calculation (excluding draft and paid)\n- Overdue invoice counting and amount\n- Top 3 customers identification and sorting\n- Handling more than 3 customers (returns exactly 3)\n- Paid invoices excluded from outstanding/topCustomers\n- Draft invoices excluded from outstanding/topCustomers\n- Partially paid invoices with reduced due amounts\n- Multiple invoices from same customer accumulate in topCustomers\n\n**Test Results:**\n- All 10 dashboard tests: \u2713 PASSING\n- Total test suite: 304 passing (plus 25 from bulk discount feature)\n- New tests successfully integrated with existing test suite\n\nThe dashboard is production-ready and provides executives/managers with key financial metrics at a glance.",
